  "major": "Depth Psychology (Community, Liberation, Indigenous, Eco-Psychologies)",
  "notes": "M.A./Ph.D. in Depth Psychology with specialization in Community, Liberation, Indigenous, Eco-Psychologies (CLIE). Classes take place in nine three-day sessions (Monday-Wednesday), approximately once each month during fall, winter, and spring (October to July). In the first and second summers, students complete fieldwork and research in their home communities or off-campus sites. In the third summer and subsequent year(s), students write dissertations in their home communities. Depth Transformative Practices (DPC 997, 0 units) in Y2 Summer requires a minimum of 60 hours of practice. Required fourth and fifth years focus on reading, research, and dissertation writing (DPC 980, 15 units).",
